# Conventional Commits

## Subject Line

Format: `{type}({scope}): {description}`

| Type | Use For |
|------|---------|
| feat | New feature |
| fix | Bug fix |
| test | Adding/updating tests |
| refactor | Code restructuring (no behaviour change) |
| docs | Documentation only |
| chore | Build, config, dependencies |
| perf | Performance improvement |

## Full Format (Agent Commits)

```
{type}({scope}): {description}

{optional body}

Tasks: {task-ids}
Agent-Session: model={model} agents={list} tokens={in}K/{out}K duration={time}

Co-Authored-By: Claude {Model} <{model}@anthropic.com>
```

## Agent-Session Line

Machine-parseable metrics:

| Field | Format | Example |
|-------|--------|---------|
| model | sonnet\|opus\|haiku | model=sonnet |
| agents | comma-separated | agents=auth-coder,auth-reviewer |
| tokens | in/out with K suffix | tokens=12.4K/8.2K |
| duration | minutes or hours | duration=45m |

## Examples

### Agent Commit

```
feat(auth): add token refresh endpoint

Tasks: AUTH-001
Agent-Session: model=sonnet agents=auth-coder tokens=8.2K/5.1K duration=32m

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet <sonnet@anthropic.com>
```

### Human Commit

```
docs(api): update OpenAPI spec for backtest endpoint

Tasks: DOC-001
```

## Shell Technique for Multi-line Commit Messages

**NEVER use `$(cat <<'EOF' ... EOF)` command substitution** — Claude Code's sandbox blocks it.

Write the message to a temp file instead:

```bash
printf 'feat(scope): subject\n\nbody line 1\nbody line 2\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n' > /tmp/commit_msg.txt
git commit -F /tmp/commit_msg.txt
rm -f /tmp/commit_msg.txt
```

For single-line messages `git commit -m "..."` is fine.

## Rules

- Max 72 chars for subject line
- Scope matches service/component name
- Description is imperative ("add" not "added")
- Tasks line references tasks.md
- Agent commits require Agent-Session and Co-Authored-By

Full template: `templates/commit-message.template.md`
